3	// Regression coverage for registering a rule version into an archive whose
4	// stored declarations have decayed. Registration only ever adds the version
5	// it was asked to add: a corrupt sibling — a missing or null field, a wrong
6	// type, an out-of-range number, an unknown or duplicate field — neither
7	// blocks a legal new registration nor gets repaired, completed, reordered
8	// or dropped by one (a missing enabled must not come back as an explicit
9	// false). And when the submitted ID is already taken by a corrupt
10	// declaration, the failure is ErrCorruptVersion naming the version and the
11	// offending rule or field — never created:false against the decayed
12	// parameters, never an overwrite, never a parameter conflict.
